Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  WACC 2 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  NAOMI R  LEEDS  M D  PHOEBE E FREER  M D  ELIZABETH A RAFFERTY  M D  Resident  Anna McDonald  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results Reason for Addendum  3  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 57 year old woman with a family history of breast cancer  She has a palpable right breast mass which is tender and very suspicious for malignancy on mammography and ultrasound imaging with a BIRADS score of 5  She also has indeterminate coarse heterogeneous microcalcifications in the left breast which are biopsied under a separate requisition  The targeted calcifications are in the specimen  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  An immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is positive in the tumor cells  supporting a diagnosis of invasive ductal carcinoma  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  BREAST  LEFT  CORE BIOPSY  HIGH GRADE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor is focally disrupted and a component of invasive ductal carcinoma cannot be excluded  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor and progesterone receptor will be reported in an ad