ons are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire nodule to the nearest margin and surrounding tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue  with a section through the nipple in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm right breast simple mastectomy which is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm wrinkled white nipple areolar complex with a centrally located 1 2cm in diameter grossly unremarkable nipple  The specimen is oriented with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The specimen has been previously dyed blue at the superior aspect  The specimen is inked as follows  Posterior   black  anterior   blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a lobulated tan yellow fatty cut surface with an abundant amount of interspersed dense gray white fibrous tissue and a large hemorrhagic area in the subareolar region  No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  The lateral aspect of the specimen is palpated  and no lymph nodes are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the central  hemorrhagic aspect of the specimen  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  RIGHT AXILLA SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 25   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06 01 32PM ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells s